WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:07.240
David, if Joe Biden gets elected and Democrats
take the Senate, what will Democrats actually

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:08.240
get done?

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:14.650
So first of all, if Biden wins and Democrats
take the Senate, it's a two year period.

00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:15.650
Okay.

00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:18.770
Democrats could then lose the Senate in 2022
or lose the House.

00:00:18.770 --> 00:00:20.110
We don't know.

00:00:20.110 --> 00:00:21.410
There's the low hanging fruit.

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:22.970
And then there's the more complicated stuff.

00:00:22.970 --> 00:00:29.980
So certainly Joe Biden will have no choice
but to use executive orders to undo a ton

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:31.180
of Trump's executive orders.

00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:34.500
Now, fortunately, many of Trump's executive
orders were just symbolic in nature.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:40.520
They didn't really do much, but a lot of executive
orders will be needed to stop the damage of

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:42.800
Trump's executive orders that do.

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:48.870
Things I do think that relatively quickly,
a Democratic Senate and Joe Biden would move

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:55.510
to try to undo as much as possible of Donald
Trump's tax reform plan that included handouts

00:00:55.510 --> 00:00:59.720
to the very rich and even provisions that
allow Donald Trump to extend his tax loss,

00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:05.000
carry forwards indefinitely rather than just
10 or 18 years, however much it was.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:09.700
But there's a really big question here, which
is that.

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:15.140
Republicans now mean, listen, they stopped
Merrick Garland in 2016 and now they will

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:17.930
probably succeed at putting in Amy CONI Barrett.

00:01:17.930 --> 00:01:19.920
They don't care about hypocrisy.

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:20.920
They will obstruct.

00:01:20.920 --> 00:01:24.060
They will do whatever Democrats if they win
the Senate.

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:28.740
And Joe Biden winds are going to have to grapple
with what to do about the filibuster, the

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:34.340
filibuster, which requires 60 Senate votes
instead of a simple majority to get a lot

00:01:34.340 --> 00:01:35.920
of things done.

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:42.520
And I don't think we are going to see major
legislative action if Republicans really suffer

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:46.670
an embarrassing defeat where Trump is made
a one term president, which is rare in American

00:01:46.670 --> 00:01:47.979
politics.

00:01:47.979 --> 00:01:50.909
And if Republicans lose the Senate, they're
gonna be hurting and they will get in the

00:01:50.909 --> 00:01:51.960
way of anything they can.

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:58.680
I don't see Obamacare being expanded the way
Joe Biden wants without a 60 votes.

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:00.310
And there's no way that they're going to get
60 votes.

00:02:00.310 --> 00:02:02.580
So the question will be, do they get rid of
the filibuster?

00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:08.660
I don't see the truck, Joe Biden's clean energy
plan going anywhere.

00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:14.379
If it depends on, you know, a Senate that
is 52 to 48 in favor of Democrats, if that's

00:02:14.379 --> 00:02:15.419
what it is.

00:02:15.419 --> 00:02:21.640
So if Democrats take control of the Senate
and they rewrite the filibuster rules, then

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:23.450
you may see more action done.

00:02:23.450 --> 00:02:25.769
Now, are they going to do that?

00:02:25.769 --> 00:02:26.769
It's risky.

00:02:26.769 --> 00:02:30.549
Barack Obama alluded to it at the funeral
of John Lewis.

00:02:30.549 --> 00:02:35.129
That's probably the highest profile support
we've seen of getting rid of the filibuster.

00:02:35.129 --> 00:02:42.180
But understand that whatever Democrats imagine
that it takes, I don't know, eight to 12 months

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:45.969
of Joe Biden's first term to get rid of the
filibuster.

00:02:45.969 --> 00:02:51.419
And then Democrats get something done in the
second year of Joe Biden's first term.

00:02:51.419 --> 00:02:56.159
And then imagine that Republicans take back
the Senate and maybe even the House, we don't

00:02:56.159 --> 00:02:58.549
know, in 2022.

00:02:58.549 --> 00:03:05.079
You have opened the door for Republicans to
use the lack of a filibuster to do ungodly

00:03:05.079 --> 00:03:06.079
things.

00:03:06.079 --> 00:03:09.639
So this is always the question is, does it
start a race to the bottom?

00:03:09.639 --> 00:03:11.019
I don't know the answer.

00:03:11.019 --> 00:03:16.510
But if somehow Democrats figured out a way
to get the votes, I believe the priorities

00:03:16.510 --> 00:03:23.079
would be to deal with coronavirus relief in
a more serious manner if depending on when

00:03:23.079 --> 00:03:24.909
that happens.

00:03:24.909 --> 00:03:28.450
Expand Obamacare in the way that Joe Biden
wants to do.

00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:30.499
New tax reform plan.

00:03:30.499 --> 00:03:31.499
Clean energy.

00:03:31.499 --> 00:03:35.059
Those would be the four that I see the most
likely that Democrats would want to tackle

00:03:35.059 --> 00:03:36.500
if given the opportunity.

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:40.629
Again, depending on what degree of a majority
do they have in the Senate or do they get

00:03:40.629 --> 00:03:41.629
rid of the filibuster?

00:03:41.629 --> 00:03:45.639
One last thing, without getting rid of the
filibuster.

00:03:45.639 --> 00:03:51.400
Democrats could still get things done if they
take the Senate, even if it's only 51, 49,

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:53.090
52, 48.

00:03:53.090 --> 00:03:56.589
But they will have to concede a ton to Republicans.

00:03:56.589 --> 00:04:03.559
They will have to pass their bills with these
horrifying, disgusting amendments that they

00:04:03.559 --> 00:04:07.829
put in there in order to get some Republican
votes.

00:04:07.829 --> 00:04:10.859
Is the country better off if that's what they
do?

00:04:10.859 --> 00:04:11.859
I don't know.

00:04:11.859 --> 00:04:14.069
You've really got to look at the specifics.

00:04:14.069 --> 00:04:17.720
We've got a great bonus show for you today
with producer Pat Forde.

00:04:17.720 --> 00:04:22.290
We will be back next week with the regular
show, the bonus show.

00:04:22.290 --> 00:04:25.280
And the vice presidential debate is next week,
Carmela.

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:28.560
I think she's going to crush, crush, crush
Mike Pence.

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:30.510
We'll see you next week if you're not a member.

00:04:30.510 --> 00:04:32.130
If you are a member.

00:04:32.130 --> 00:04:33.660
Enjoy the bonus show coming up right after
this.

